The computer used by Mr. Werx is housed at Carleton University but is not
owned by the University.  It is owned by the National Capital FreeNet
Inc., a separate not for profit corporation.  It is not subject to
University rules and regulations.  Under the NCD User Agreement, which Mr.
Werxa signed, item 2 states: 

"That the National Capital FreeNet reserves the right to review
any material stored in files or programs to which users have access and
will edit or remove any material which the Board, in its sole descretion,
believes may be unlawful, obscene or abusive, or otherwise objectionable."

Thus, the NCF has the right to do what you have acused them of.  I point
out, however, NO MATERIAL HAS BEEN REMOVED FROM INDIVIDUAL ACCOUNTS.  We
did remove copies of the NY Times K-H aricle from newsgroup files because
it violated the publication ban and violated copyright (the Times
subsequently posted a notice of objection about the violation of their
copyright).  


